One clarification on decoration sizing:

I want DECORATIONS to be independently resizable in BOTH directions.

This is not just "make them taller."

Each decoration resource should support:

    W = horizontal size
    H = vertical size

Examples:

    1 × 1   normal
    2 × 1   wide bush / table / barrier
    3 × 1   very wide prop
    1 × 2   tall prop
    1 × 3   tree / column / sign
    2 × 2   large square prop
    3 × 2   large wide prop

The current resource model already has:

    d.w
    d.h

and the current UI already exposes separate W / H controls.

KEEP that architecture.

Do not collapse sizing into one uniform SCALE value.

==================================================
EXPECTED RENDER SEMANTICS
==================================================

Height and width must affect the final SPRPOS2 rectangle independently.

Current generator approach is directionally correct:

    H controls projected sprite height
    W controls projected sprite width

For example:

    1 × 3

must render substantially taller while keeping roughly normal width.

    3 × 1

must render substantially wider while keeping roughly normal height.

    3 × 2

must render both wider AND taller.

Do not interpret W/H as map occupancy.

The decoration remains ONE placed anchor in the 28×28 decor placement layer.

W/H only controls how large that billboard appears in the game.

==================================================
IMPORTANT DISTINCTION
==================================================

"Extend horizontally and vertically" means VISUAL sprite dimensions.

It does NOT mean:

    occupy several map cells
    duplicate the sprite into adjacent cells
    create several decor records
    change collision automatically
    stretch the atlas source rectangle

The source art remains one sprite frame.

SPRTEX selects the same source artwork.

SPRP0S2 / SPRPOS2 destination rectangle stretches that artwork to the desired
world-visible proportions.

