==================================================
TEST MATRIX
==================================================

Use one clearly asymmetric test sprite and render four copies at the SAME
distance:

    A = 1×1
    B = 2×1
    C = 1×2
    D = 2×2

Expected:

    A normal

    B:
        same height as A
        ~2× width

    C:
        same width as A
        ~2× height

    D:
        ~2× width
        ~2× height

This test is much better than comparing only 1×1 vs 1×3 because it proves
horizontal and vertical scaling independently.

==================================================
DO NOT CHANGE THE MATHS AGAIN BLINDLY
==================================================

The current emitted BASIC already produces materially different SPRPOS2
rectangles for different W/H values.

Before changing the generator again, determine whether the emulator actually
honours destination rectangle scaling.

If the emulator renders all four test cases identically despite different
SPRP0S2/SPRP0S2 arguments, treat that as an emulator limitation until hardware
testing says otherwise.

Hardware remains the source of truth.
